From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 10:54:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 958: the wallet debit runs after the answer is sent, not
 before

0235's [post-run] laps (44 runs, 09:25-10:52Z): after the tool loop, a
median 4.0 s, of which the wallet debit was 1.17 s on every run. That is
eight database round trips, and nothing in the answer depends on them. The
debit now starts inside processChat without being awaited, and comes back
with the result as afterReply. The thread route awaits it right after
emitRunComplete, still inside the run's in-flight mark, so a deploy drain
still waits for it and the conversation is released only after it. Its code
is unchanged (moved, not edited): the moderation guard, the payer rule and
the error log are as before. The answer reaches the owner about 1.2 s sooner.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
